  "descriptionMarkdown": "Spoilage is a primary challenge on Gleba, as it penalizes overproduction and complicates automation. To achieve reliable automation and maximize freshness, this blueprint book provides:\n\n- **Stable producers**: Agriculture towers with output rates precisely controlled via circuits\n- **Stable consumers**: Yumako and Jellynut processors that consume a fixed number of fruits and run forever, regardless of whether their outputs (Yumako mash and jelly) are being consumed\n\nAs a result, Yumako and Jellynut production can be strictly balanced, maximizing freshness throughout the supply chain.\n\nThe Yumako processor is generally my first factory after landing on Gleba as it provides a stable source of fuel and electronics. \n\nThe processors also integrate the feature of building artificial soils using excess seeds; put some landfill manually into the dedicated chests.",
